[10.009719, "o", "\r\n--- CLAUDE.md guidance (add to /work/CLAUDE.md) ---\r\n## Process Enforcement\r\n\r\nThis project uses turnstile for process enforcement (currently **monitor** mode).\r\n\r\n**Before editing any code, start the appropriate process:**\r\n\r\n| Task | Command |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| Structured bug fix workflow: reproduce, diagnose, fix, verify | `process_start(\"bug-fix\", {\"bug_summary\": \"...\"})` |\r\n| Structured review of a changeset or pull request | `process_start(\"code-review\", {\"branch\": \"...\"})` |\r\n| Design and validate a new turnstile process definition | `process_start(\"create-process\", {\"name\": \"...\", \"purpose\": \"...\"})` |\r\n| Structured decision-making process producing an auditable record of context, options, and rationale | `process_start(\"decision-record\", {\"decision_title\": \"...\"})` |\r\n| Standard feature development workflow | `process_start(\"feature-development\", {\"feature_name\": \"...\"})` |\r\n| Structured peer review with role handoff: submit, review, revise, accept | `process_start(\"peer-review\", {\"artifact\": \"...\"})` |\r\n| Update the project README to reflect the current state of the codebase | `process_start(\"readme-update\", {\"reason\": \"...\"})` |\r\n| Prepare, validate, and ship a versioned release | `process_start(\"release\", {\"version\": \"...\"})` |\r\n| Structured investigation using the scientific method: observe, hypothesize, test, conclude | `process_start(\"scientific-method\", {\"observation\": \"...\"})` |\r\n| Security-focused peer review with OWASP and threat modeling guidance | `process_start(\"security-review\", {\"artifact\": \"...\"})` |\r\n| Time-boxed investigation with a written outcome | `process_start(\"spike\", {\"question\": \"...\"})` |\r\n\r\nUse `process_status()` to check active instances. Use `process_transition()` to advance through states. The enforcement guard will remind you of your current state on every file edit.\r\n\r\nStates with `permissions.edit: false` restrict file edits until you transition to an implementation state. Follow the validation gates; they surface useful context.\r\n--- end guidance ---\r\n\r\nAdd the above block to your project's CLAUDE.md, placing it where it fits best in the document structure.\r\n"]
[10.03541, "o", "\r\n$ turnstile list\r\n"]
[10.435264, "o", "  feature-development v1.3.0 - Standard feature development workflow\r\n  create-process v1.0.0 - Design and validate a new turnstile process definition\r\n  readme-update v1.0.0 - Update the project README to reflect the current state of the codebase\r\n  bug-fix v1.2.0 - Structured bug fix workflow: reproduce, diagnose, fix, verify\r\n  code-review v1.1.0 - Structured review of a changeset or pull request\r\n  release v1.1.0 - Prepare, validate, and ship a versioned release\r\n  spike v1.0.0 - Time-boxed investigation with a written outcome\r\n  scientific-method v1.0.0 - Structured investigation using the scientific method: observe, hypothesize, test, conclude\r\n  decision-record v1.0.0 - Structured decision-making process producing an auditable record of context, options, and rationale\r\n  peer-review v1.0.0 - Structured peer review with role handoff: submit, review, revise, accept\r\n  security-review v1.0.0 - Security-focused peer review with OWASP and threat modeling guidance\r\n"]
